WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:35.490
<b>Scrap Heap
Fabriophase
Egghead</b>

3
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:35.740
This is awesome!

4
00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:38.520
Guys, check it out!

5
00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:40.520
Haha!

6
00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:41.640
I'm like Sanji!

7
00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:43.120
What happened to your head?

8
00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.400
It used to be so big and tall, like
you had a giant light bulb growing

9
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.380
out of your skull.

10
00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:48.520
My head?

11
00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:50.190
Oh!

12
00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:54.140
Well, it had grown quite
long you see, so I cut it.

13
00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:56.780
What, like you had it snipped
off at the frikken barber?

14
00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:57.950
Then I had to.

15
00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:59.530
What else was I to do?

16
00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.740
When I last saw you,
it was so big.

17
00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.790
I was almost as tall as a giant!

18
00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.620
I heard it was big,
but that sounds ridiculous.

19
00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:07.920
It was like a balloon.

20
00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:12.600
You cut your head
but you're still alive?

21
00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.030
How is that even possible?

22
00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:20.560
Well, you see, my young friends,
I have a brain.

23
00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:23.050
I bit my tongue.

24
00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:23.860
Oh, no.

25
00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:24.800
My poor tongue.

26
00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:26.410
Old man, you okay?

27
00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:33.240
You see, my young friends,
I've eaten the brain fruit.

28
00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.560
It allows me to absorb
limitless knowledge.

29
00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:41.460
But the more my brain knows,
the more it grows and grows and grows.

30
00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:46.150
On top of my natural genius,
I possess an unlimited data bank.

31
00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.790
Thus, I have the world's
largest brain.

32
00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.700
And it grows larger
and larger every day.

33
00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:52.720
Wait, what?

34
00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.160
Then where is it?

35
00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.490
That sounds insane.

36
00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:56.410
You lost me.

37
00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:00.370
I get it.

38
00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.440
You cut your brain out
so now you're stupid.

39
00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.900
Do not trifle
with a genius, boy!

40
00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:09.080
This apple here is an antenna.

41
00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.930
Connected to what?

42
00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:12.840
Look at the structure
up there.

43
00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:19.530
The inside of that egg doesn't
say Punk Records just for fun.

44
00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.670
That is where my enormous
brain is stored.

45
00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.370
It's really that big?

46
00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:28.360
Even when I'm far away,
I remain connected to it.

47
00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:31.380
Thanks to the brain waves received
through this apple antenna.

48
00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:32.500
That's so cool!

49
00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.310
So are you a doctor
of medicine too, Vegapunk?

50
00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:38.070
You bet, little buddy.

51
00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:44.110
You met a girl when you came here,
who also called herself Vegapunk, yes?

52
00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:46.090
Huh?

53
00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:47.940
Yeah, she punched me in the face.

54
00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:50.790
That girl is one of my clones.

55
00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.550
There are six on the island.

56
00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:53.180
Two ninjas?

57
00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:56.440
It's Shadow Clone Jutsu!

58
00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:03.450
Each of them has a unique talent
and plays a necessary role.

59
00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:06.710
Shaka is calm
and conscientious.

60
00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:09.350
<b>Shaka the Just</b>
<b>AAAAAAAAAA</b>

61
00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:12.510
Lilith has no morals
and is willing to plunder.

62
00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:15.530
<b>Lilith the Evil</b>
<b>AAAAAAAAAAAAAA</b>

63
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:17.800
Edison is bursting with ideas.

64
00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:20.450
<b>Edison the Visionary AAAAAAAAAAAAAA</b>

65
00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:23.950
The wise Pythagoras
follows the path of reason.

66
00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:26.750
<b>Pythagoras the Wise AAAAAAAAAAAAAA</b>

67
00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:29.840
Atlas is here when
violence is the answer.

68
00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:32.540
<b>Atlas the Enraged AAAAAAAAAAAAAA</b>

69
00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:35.760
And the greedy York
eats poops and sleeps.

70
00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.800
<b>York the Greedy AAAAAAAAAAAAAA</b>

71
00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:43.570
They are me, in the sense that
they comprise my personality.

72
00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.900
But they do six
times the work.

73
00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.310
Oh, I'm confused.

74
00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:54.230
Once daily, they synchronize their experiences
and newly acquired knowledge

75
00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:56.180
by accessing Punk Records.

76
00:04:56.260 --> 00:05:00.000
Their personalities and missions are
different, making each of them unique.

77
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.410
They are uniquely
useful for my research.

78
00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.380
All of you share
the same brain?

79
00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:07.690
This is far beyond
my comprehension.

80
00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.920
Just think of it as us
visiting the same library.

81
00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:16.810
Let me give you an example.

82
00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:22.900
Imagine if the rest of the world accessed
the database and read the information

83
00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:24.390
contained in my brain.

84
00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:29.690
It would be as if all mankind
had acquired my knowledge.

85
00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:30.470
Wow.

86
00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:37.470
Then what if those people updated Punk
Records with their personal discoveries,

87
00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:38.530
just as I do?

88
00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:45.720
Why, we could create a sea
of knowledge, far exceeding my own.

89
00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:48.960
A library of the human
experience.

90
00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:52.920
Like a super brain,
shared by all humanity.

91
00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.930
Does that mean I could study
medicine from all over the world?

92
00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:57.010
That's the idea.

93
00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:02.650
I have no idea
what's going on!

94
00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:09.130
But what happens when different
ideologies enter the brain?

95
00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.460
Won't that cause issues?

96
00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:13.150
A fine question,
first son of the sea.

97
00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:18.510
And yet, if we never dare to take a chance,
then science will never advance.

98
00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:22.950
Of course you
would think that way.

99
00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:24.430
You bastard!

100
00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:27.000
You'll sacrifice anything
for your research!

101
00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:28.480
Or anyone, even!

102
00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:29.360
Yeah!

103
00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:32.530
Like my father.

104
00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.920
You turned him into
a heartless machine!

105
00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:39.070
Stop, Bonney!

106
00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:41.690
That beam saber is
a failed invention!

107
00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:42.500
Shut up!

108
00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.580
It'll kill you just fine.

109
00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:46.130
Please calm down, Bonney.

110
00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:47.680
You must think this through.

111
00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.110
I know that you're angry.

112
00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:52.080
But killing him will make
far too many enemies.

113
00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:53.710
I don't give a damn.

114
00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:56.380
Now, you're gonna
turn my father back.

115
00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:59.690
Or I swear, I'm gonna slice
your head off, right here!

116
00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:00.470
And now!

117
00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.370
Please turn off
the switch, quickly!

118
00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:11.690
It's fun.

119
00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:14.730
But it attracts
a swarm of bugs!

120
00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.130
Bonney!

121
00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:29.580
Hey, Bonney!

122
00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.110
Bonney!

123
00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:31.840
Wake up!

124
00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:35.320
Check this out!

125
00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:36.200
Put that down!

126
00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:37.480
She'll freak out!

127
00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.560
What happens if
she dies of shock?

128
00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:44.300
If that weapon wasn't a failure,
I would likely be dead.

129
00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:46.300
But it's no wonder.

130
00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:47.560
I can blame her.

131
00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:50.590
It's only natural that
she'd want to kill me.

132
00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.820
Oh, there was something
I wanted to ask.

133
00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:56.140
I heard you came here
from the land of Wano.

134
00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:56.920
Mm-hmm.

135
00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:00.790
I also heard there were
two dragons there.

136
00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:03.030
Kaido and someone else.

137
00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:03.910
Oh, yeah.

138
00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:05.740
That's my friend Momo.

139
00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:08.920
I see.

140
00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:13.430
It seems he ate a failed
synthetic devil fruit I left at Punk Hazard.

141
00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:14.730
Oh, that's cool.

142
00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:15.570
Wait.

143
00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:17.010
How did it fail?

144
00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:19.370
It wasn't from lack of effort.

145
00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:21.800
I developed that
project myself.

146
00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:25.760
Twenty years of hard work and a whole
mountain of research money.

147
00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:28.990
I tried to make a fruit from
Kaido's Bloodline Elements.

148
00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:32.700
But in the end, I couldn't get
the composition quite right.

149
00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:37.060
Oh, so that's why he was
able to transform like Kaido.

150
00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:38.400
It wasn't a failure.

151
00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:40.650
He breathes fire
and he's real strong.

152
00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:42.970
He protects the land
of Wano now.

153
00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:45.480
You did a really
good job, Appleguy.

154
00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:47.340
What is the dragon's color?

155
00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.340
Pink-white.

156
00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:50.930
Failure!

157
00:08:51.770 --> 00:08:53.580
An utter failure!

158
00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:55.480
What's wrong with him?

159
00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:57.510
He's a genius.

160
00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:59.540
But he's also quite
the perfectionist.

161
00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:01.540
Oh, yeah.

162
00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:07.690
Hey, old man!

163
00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.240
Can you get this to move?

164
00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:11.320
You're the one who
made it, right?

165
00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:14.990
I didn't make it.

166
00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:19.720
This is the legendary iron giant that
is said to have attacked Mary Geoise.

167
00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:22.710
200 years ago.

168
00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:24.420
And attacked Mary Geoise?

169
00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:25.390
That's insane!

170
00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:26.630
Indubitably!

171
00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:30.840
This monstrosity was built...
900 years ago!

172
00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:32.170
Wait, what? Nine hundred?

173
00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:33.390
Forgive my skepticism.

174
00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:34.490
But how can that be?

175
00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:35.600
Wow!

176
00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:37.610
You're really special, big guy!

177
00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:40.030
So how did you
attack Mary Geoise?

178
00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:40.780
Cannons?

179
00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:41.590
Lasers?

180
00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:43.010
Come on!

181
00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:44.530
Wake up, Robonosuke!

182
00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:45.590
Do robot stuff!

183
00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:47.290
Get up, boy!

184
00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:48.130
Shoot lasers!

185
00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:48.940
Let's go!

186
00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.280
That is an antique,
you troglodyte!

187
00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:54.510
Quite the fascinating story.

188
00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:57.440
But tell me, why would the iron
giant attack Mary Geoise?

189
00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:58.780
A fine question!

190
00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:03.440
I haven't the faintest clue.

191
00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:04.690
Oh.

192
00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:31.900
I heard that it ran out of power,
and no damage was done.

193
00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:40.320
Regardless, I imagine its very existence
was shocking to the scientists of the time.

194
00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:42.310
It's extraordinary... beyond.

195
00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:45.140
Beyond any
technology in its era.

196
00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:49.390
Hmm. Hundreds of years later,
I'd say this is still quite the shock!

197
00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:50.890
We were trying
to wake it up, but.

198
00:10:50.890 --> 00:10:53.140
It might be better
if it stays like this.

199
00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:56.270
It could be dangerous.

200
00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:59.610
No one knows where this iron
giant came from, after all.

201
00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:03.540
It's unclear what it was trying to do,
or what it was capable of.

202
00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:08.730
As for the World Government,
predictably, they ordered its destruction.

203
00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:11.890
But the scientists
of that age protected it.

204
00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:14.870
They hid it away,
where no one could find it.

205
00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:17.820
And to this day,
no one knows it is here.

206
00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.600
Not even
the Government itself.

207
00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.640
Ugh.

208
00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:27.790
Anyway, I'm surprised you
made it to this junk yard.

209
00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:30.430
The entrance to here
looks like a normal wall.

210
00:11:30.510 --> 00:11:32.980
I can't imagine how
you found your way in.

211
00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:38.860
Where'd he go?

212
00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:40.070
He just...

213
00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:41.650
Vanished!

214
00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:43.790
I got turned old.

215
00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:45.430
My brain wasn't workin' right.

216
00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:48.660
We were lost and hiding!
And we looked terrible!

217
00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:49.250
Fair.

218
00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:50.600
That sounds concerning.

219
00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:51.940
<b>Labophase
Egghead</b>

220
00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:52.300
Two hundred years ago.

221
00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:55.080
That's the year fishmen were
granted citizens' rights.

222
00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:57.260
I don't know how
the robot works,

223
00:11:57.340 --> 00:12:00.290
Are you saying it climbed
all the way up the Red Line?

224
00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:01.600
So it seems.

225
00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:02.710
Am I crazy?

226
00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:06.230
Or does that thing look an awful lot
like the robot that brought us here?

227
00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:07.100
That's right.

228
00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:08.480
It's no coincidence.

229
00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:11.380
Vegaforce-01 was
modeled after the iron giant.

230
00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:15.550
But even with all my knowledge,
there was one thing I couldn't replicate.

231
00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:18.110
But you're the brainiest
bro on the entire planet!

232
00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:20.610
What the hell does it
take to stump you?

233
00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:21.890
The power source.

234
00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:26.760
The way the iron giant used energy
defies our modern understanding of science.

235
00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:32.550
By the way, I'm glad Luffy
and the others are all right,

236
00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:33.910
but who's that woman?

237
00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:35.390
Uh... That's Jewelry Bonney.

238
00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:36.360
She's a pirate.

239
00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:37.540
Wait a second,

240
00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:40.430
That's not the same little
girl we saved earlier, is it?

241
00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:41.430
Huh?

242
00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:44.450
I'm sorry, what is going
on with Vegapunk's head?

243
00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:46.940
Is Bonney okay?

244
00:12:47.020 --> 00:12:47.870
What gives?

245
00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:49.800
Poor Bonney.

246
00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:51.770
She's been through so much.

247
00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:53.070
Yeah, cause of you!

248
00:12:53.150 --> 00:12:54.230
She should get to hit you!

249
00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:56.730
What the hell do you
know about this, huh?!

250
00:12:56.810 --> 00:12:57.950
Not a thing!

251
00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:04.580
When she wakes up, there's
something important I need to give her.

252
00:13:05.230 --> 00:13:07.990
But first, I have
a favor to ask.

253
00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:08.770
Huh?

254
00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:11.860
It's extremely fortunate that you
showed up here when you did.

255
00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:13.720
You might even call it fate.

256
00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:15.050
What do you mean?

257
00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:17.780
My dear boy, I need you to take me
away from Egghead.

258
00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:19.820
I re-quasar your help!

259
00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:20.730
Huh?

260
00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:32.150
This is Cipher Pol speaking.

261
00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:34.670
Grant us entry
to the island at once.

262
00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:36.400
Do you copy?

263
00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:37.290
I said, this is Cipher Pol...

264
00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:38.240
Oh, no, no.

265
00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:39.030
This is bad.

266
00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:40.640
This is very bad!

267
00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:41.880
Attack!

268
00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:55.220
Should have trained
their pets better.

269
00:13:58.240 --> 00:13:59.790
We received a report.

270
00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:02.270
It seems that Jewelry
Bonney is here on Egghead.

271
00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:03.840
Well, that's convenient.

272
00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:05.840
Don't let her escape again.

273
00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:09.280
She's outlived her usefulness.

274
00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:11.270
Be sure to kill her on sight.

275
00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:15.140
Shaka, a-a Government
ship just arrived!

276
00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:18.230
What?

277
00:14:18.230 --> 00:14:18.980
Why?

278
00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:20.490
You pirates need to hide!

279
00:14:20.570 --> 00:14:23.500
If the government finds out
you're here, we're all doomed!

280
00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:25.110
No complaints from us.

281
00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:28.290
We're not lookin' to pick a fight
with them, just to be clear.

282
00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:29.450
As you shouldn't!

283
00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:31.320
They have CP0 with them.

284
00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:33.540
Even Rob Lucci is on board!

285
00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:35.480
What?

286
00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:36.810
Rob Lucci?

287
00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:41.060
Well, I guess it's time
to feed the cat.

288
00:14:41.140 --> 00:14:41.520
Huh?

289
00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:42.400
Oh, and look!

290
00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:44.210
We've got five
tuna steaks here!

291
00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:44.830
Come on!

292
00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:46.550
Let's hand these
goofballs over.

293
00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:52.000
Let me out of these shoes
right now, you sick bastards!

294
00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:53.380
No! Why is he here?

295
00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:55.440
I thought he quit his job!

296
00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:56.770
We can't let him get in!

297
00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:59.080
He better not even try!

298
00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:01.410
I'll send him packin' myself!

299
00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:02.420
Don't worry, Robin.

300
00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:03.320
You're safe with us!

301
00:15:03.320 --> 00:15:05.460
We'll beat him as many
times as it takes!

302
00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:06.360
Thank you.

303
00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:09.030
Officially, they're here
to return the seraphim.

304
00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:09.710
Huh?

305
00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:11.800
Tell them to leave it
and send them away.

306
00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:13.000
Excuse me?

307
00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:15.660
We're going to bar
the Government's entry.

308
00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:16.890
Lock down the island!

309
00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:17.790
Huh?

310
00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:27.280
Whoa!

311
00:15:27.340 --> 00:15:28.040
Hold up!

312
00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:36.290
<b>Kamabakka Queendom
Grand Line</b>

313
00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:34.460
Wait!

314
00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:34.960
Stop!

315
00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:36.350
You're still under repair!

316
00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:38.140
You can't start moving now!

317
00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:45.930
Dragon, help!

318
00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:47.850
There's something
wrong with Kuma!

319
00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:48.730
Huh?

320
00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:49.890
Kuma.

321
00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:51.200
Stop, Kuma!

322
00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:52.680
What happened?

323
00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:56.670
Maybe the Navy is still
giving him orders somehow!

324
00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:06.010
What do you need?

325
00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:07.150
Let us help you!

326
00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:10.230
Can you at least tell us
where you're trying to go?

327
00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:19.770
What started this?

328
00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:20.670
I don't know!

329
00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:22.440
He just got up
out of the blue!

330
00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:25.310
He's not supposed
to have any free will left.

331
00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:27.850
Stop it!

332
00:16:27.850 --> 00:16:29.620
You're gonna hurt yourself!

333
00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:32.280
Come back here, Kuma!

334
00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:33.600
Where are you going?

335
00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:47.940
We need you, Kuma!

336
00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:49.710
You're part of our family!

337
00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:52.870
We have to stick together
and see our battle through!

338
00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:00.990
No! Kuma, stop!

339
00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:02.070
Please, don't go!

340
00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:12.200
He's gone.

341
00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:19.920
Thank you for returning
our seraphim to us.

342
00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:25.290
Unfortunately, your request for entry is
denied, so just drop him off and go, please.

343
00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:26.920
Uh, no need to worry!

344
00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:29.680
S-Bear can return home
on his own two feet.

345
00:17:29.760 --> 00:17:31.720
And from there,
you'll have to forgive us.

346
00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:34.470
But we are so busy,
we can barely think straight.

347
00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:38.330
So, um, order S-Bear to return
and you can call it a day!

348
00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.490
Mission complete!

349
00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:40.920
Thank you for your service.

350
00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:41.790
Whoa there!

351
00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:44.060
You can't just leave
us out in the cold!

352
00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:46.170
Seems they're on to us.

353
00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:48.600
Aren't you at least going
to invite us in for a cup of tea?

354
00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:49.990
We've been sailing for days.

355
00:17:49.990 --> 00:17:51.260
We're freezing out here!

356
00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:55.290
Naval Branch G-14 is
right around the corner.

357
00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:57.460
I'm sure they'll welcome
you with open arms.

358
00:17:57.460 --> 00:17:59.180
Am I speaking to Vegapunk?

359
00:17:59.260 --> 00:17:59.940
Uh. Yes?

360
00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:01.960
I have a question
for you, Doctor.

361
00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:05.650
What do you know about
the Egghead disappearances?

362
00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:06.490
Huh?

363
00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:09.850
Disappearances?

364
00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:11.200
I beg your pardon?

365
00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:13.080
I'm afraid I don't follow.

366
00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:18.200
Two months ago, Cipher Pol Number
5's ship vanished into thin air.

367
00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:20.990
A month ago,
it was Cipher Pol Number 7.

368
00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:23.600
Two weeks ago,
Cipher Pol Number 8.

369
00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:26.020
Quite the strange coincidence.

370
00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:30.450
In fact, not one Government ship that has
visited Egghead in the past two months has

371
00:18:30.530 --> 00:18:31.200
returned.

372
00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:34.210
I was hoping you might be able
to shed some light on why.

373
00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:36.140
Hmm?

374
00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:37.660
– Huh?
– Hm?

375
00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:40.110
Well, I am so sorry to hear

376
00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:43.130
that, but rest assured,
we don't have them here.

377
00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:46.630
My records show that all vessels
have shipped out in ship-shape.

378
00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:47.540
Hey!

379
00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:49.620
What exactly are
you implying?

380
00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:53.840
Are you trying to say we've been messing
with those ships, you overgrown housecat?

381
00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:54.790
Go to hell!

382
00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:57.770
Lilith, I know you're evil,
but please don't antagonize me!

383
00:18:57.770 --> 00:18:58.340
Ah!

384
00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:00.990
You are gonna look so
stupid when I open this port!

385
00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:01.560
Lilith!

386
00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:02.260
No!

387
00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:03.200
Back off, Pythagoras!

388
00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:03.980
I gotta fight!

389
00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:06.390
Ah, well, like I said, no ships here,
but we appreciate your visit.

390
00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:07.160
Goodbye!

391
00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:10.420
Fine then. If you insist.

392
00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:15.310
Nice try, but I doubt
they're going to budge.

393
00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:17.150
Shall we move on to Plan B?

394
00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.390
Everyone, get ready.

395
00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:22.120
We're going to abandon ship!

396
00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:25.150
We'll use the seraphim.

397
00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:26.660
S-Bear follows our orders.

398
00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:28.950
We'll have it transport
us to Egghead.

399
00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:32.720
We're sacrificing the ship.

400
00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:36.570
As soon as we leave, it will fall
prey to the Sea Beast Weapons.

401
00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:39.220
Yes, sir!

402
00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:42.880
That's a tad bit risky,
don't you think?

403
00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:46.240
Impatience isn't attractive
in a man, you know.

404
00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:49.370
If you wanna be swallowed by
the sea, you're welcome to stay.

405
00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:51.020
And threats, too?

406
00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:52.580
Let's go.

407
00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:10.830
Do you wanna leave
this place, old man?

408
00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:11.700
But it's your lab.

409
00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:13.730
I thought you liked living here.

410
00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:15.160
What's not to like?

411
00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:18.250
Why, I'm creating
the future itself here!

412
00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:22.400
I can use Government facilities
and funds however I please.

413
00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:26.320
And thus, my research has
continued at an extraordinary pace!

414
00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:29.230
You've seen only a small
fraction of my work!

415
00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:35.470
My brain is a fountain of ideas
that never stops flowing!

416
00:20:35.550 --> 00:20:37.120
But there's not enough time.

417
00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:38.090
Nor enough help,

418
00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:41.400
Nor enough money to make
my true dream a reality!

419
00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:45.470
You mean you're planning
something even bigger?

420
00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:47.020
You want to know what it is?

421
00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:49.180
You bet we do!

422
00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:53.650
When it happens, the whole
universe will know my name!

423
00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:55.490
Ooh!

424
00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:57.120
Is it another big robot?

425
00:20:57.200 --> 00:20:58.140
Tell us, please!

426
00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:00.220
Very well, then!

427
00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:01.700
It's really quite simple.

428
00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:04.510
I will use science
to squash inequality!

429
00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:09.070
I will create a world where
free energy is provided to all!

430
00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:13.400
That's not the reaction
I expected.

431
00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:14.230
I don't know.

432
00:21:14.310 --> 00:21:15.950
Free stuff's cool, I guess.

433
00:21:16.030 --> 00:21:18.680
That would be a worthwhile
endeavor if you could achieve it.

434
00:21:18.680 --> 00:21:21.070
Most wars are
fought over energy.

435
00:21:21.150 --> 00:21:23.280
We might be able
to achieve world peace,

436
00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:25.090
but resources are too limited.

437
00:21:25.170 --> 00:21:26.410
Are they limited?

438
00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:28.810
Or is it mankind
who is limited?

439
00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:31.690
Energy is everywhere!

440
00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:33.760
You can feel it!

441
00:21:33.840 --> 00:21:34.700
In the air!

442
00:21:35.110 --> 00:21:36.230
In the ground!

443
00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:37.740
It's all around us!

444
00:21:38.460 --> 00:21:40.060
It's simply overflowing!

445
00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:43.510
The world is full of energy!

446
00:21:46.170 --> 00:21:50.210
All we need to do is convert
it into tangible power!

447
00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:53.140
Inequality will become
a thing of the past!

448
00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:55.850
Wars will come to an end!

449
00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:02.820
With the power of science,
we can make this world a utopia!

450
00:22:06.390 --> 00:22:08.320
Still not interested?

451
00:22:08.400 --> 00:22:11.980
No, I think it's really cool that
you wanna make people happy.

452
00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:14.340
But hero stuff just
isn't my thing.

453
00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:17.090
Anyway, you never said
why you wanna leave.

454
00:22:17.170 --> 00:22:19.110
Well, I have a problem.

455
00:22:19.190 --> 00:22:23.710
The more I try to create this energy,
the further I delve into lost history.

456
00:22:24.420 --> 00:22:26.500
For example, I can't help it.

457
00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:30.040
I can't help but to look to our giant
mechanical friend here and wonder what

458
00:22:30.040 --> 00:22:32.800
kind of ancient energy
source powered him.

459
00:22:32.880 --> 00:22:36.670
It is the nature of a scientist
to remain curious, after all.

460
00:22:37.150 --> 00:22:42.140
So I took a little peek into history
and unraveled some forbidden truths.

461
00:22:43.060 --> 00:22:48.670
I was only carrying on my friend's will, but it
took me deep into dangerous waters.

462
00:22:52.760 --> 00:22:53.560
Oh.

463
00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:55.230
What?

464
00:22:59.060 --> 00:23:00.190
And that's my story!

465
00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:01.870
I just love learning too much!

466
00:23:01.950 --> 00:23:03.680
Now, the Government
will erase me!

467
00:23:03.760 --> 00:23:04.600
Just like...

468
00:23:06.910 --> 00:23:08.030
This can't be good.

469
00:23:08.110 --> 00:23:09.820
It must be CP0.

470
00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:11.400
Wait, 0?

471
00:23:11.480 --> 00:23:13.610
They're a spy
organization directly

472
00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:16.220
under the orders
of the Celestial Dragons.

473
00:23:16.300 --> 00:23:17.910
I thought they
were called CP9.

474
00:23:17.990 --> 00:23:19.920
Did they change
their name, or what?

475
00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:21.920
CP0 is a higher rank.

476
00:23:22.550 --> 00:23:24.470
You rarely see
them make a move.

477
00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:29.110
But when they do, it means that
the course of history is about to change.

478
00:23:29.600 --> 00:23:30.480
Ah!

479
00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:33.790
This place is incredible!

480
00:23:33.870 --> 00:23:35.860
Why, I've never
seen anything like it!

481
00:23:35.940 --> 00:23:36.880
It's unreal!

482
00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:39.510
Like we stepped
straight into the future!

483
00:23:39.590 --> 00:23:41.650
I'm getting a little
fired up here!

484
00:23:42.200 --> 00:23:44.030
What's Cipher Pol doing here?

485
00:23:44.110 --> 00:23:46.300
And why aren't they
wearing their black suits?

486
00:23:46.300 --> 00:23:47.100
How bizarre.

487
00:23:47.180 --> 00:23:49.910
Don't they usually come
in through the port?

488
00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:50.820
Hey, guys!

489
00:23:50.900 --> 00:23:51.390
Hm?

490
00:23:51.390 --> 00:23:55.030
We just got a report that two of the Sea
Beast Weapons were attacked at the shore!

491
00:23:55.030 --> 00:23:55.730
Huh?

492
00:23:55.740 --> 00:24:00.240
Don't tell me... does that
mean they're intruders?

493
00:24:04.010 --> 00:24:06.530
Shaka! CP0 is
on the island!

494
00:24:08.270 --> 00:24:09.390
Gah! We're too late!

495
00:24:09.470 --> 00:24:10.300
They're here!

496
00:24:10.900 --> 00:24:12.910
Lucci's bein' a giant
pain in the ass.

497
00:24:12.990 --> 00:24:15.210
What else is new?
Cat bastard.

498
00:24:15.290 --> 00:24:16.240
Come on.

499
00:24:16.320 --> 00:24:18.390
Give it up already, Lucci!

500
00:24:22.770 --> 00:24:24.010
Ugh. I'm still stuck!

501
00:24:24.090 --> 00:24:26.910
Would you fix these stupid
future shoes already?

502
00:24:27.290 --> 00:24:28.750
I need my damn feet!

503
00:24:28.830 --> 00:24:30.770
How else can I
keep Robin safe?

504
00:24:32.020 --> 00:24:34.140
How did they come
ashore so quickly?

505
00:24:45.570 --> 00:24:47.570
Well, definitely not by ship,

506
00:24:47.650 --> 00:24:49.130
That's for darn sure.

507
00:24:49.210 --> 00:24:52.870
Seems they realized the Sea Beast Weapons
would attack their ship as soon

508
00:24:52.950 --> 00:24:54.250
as they refused to leave.

509
00:24:54.330 --> 00:24:57.980
They must have used
the seraphim's Paw-Paw power to fly here!

510
00:24:58.060 --> 00:24:59.330
What should we do?

511
00:24:59.410 --> 00:25:00.760
How resourceful.

512
00:25:01.230 --> 00:25:05.000
They must really want a fight
if they're sacrificing their ship.

513
00:25:05.080 --> 00:25:06.010
Very well.

514
00:25:06.090 --> 00:25:07.670
If that's what you desire.

515
00:25:08.230 --> 00:25:09.330
Sound the alarm!

516
00:25:09.410 --> 00:25:11.370
We need to evacuate
the citizens!

517
00:25:11.830 --> 00:25:12.630
Roger that!

518
00:25:24.200 --> 00:25:26.080
Tell Atlas to return to the lab!

519
00:25:27.050 --> 00:25:29.420
Prepare all of the seraphim
for combat!

520
00:25:30.400 --> 00:25:31.980
Sentomaru will lead them!

521
00:25:40.870 --> 00:25:43.050
Releasing seraphim
number one.

522
00:25:43.730 --> 00:25:44.050
S-Hawk.

523
00:25:44.050 --> 00:25:44.750
S-Hawk!

524
00:25:49.890 --> 00:25:51.940
Releasing seraphim
number three.

525
00:25:52.640 --> 00:25:53.510
S-Snake.

526
00:25:54.070 --> 00:25:57.030
S-Snake!

527
00:25:57.870 --> 00:25:59.810
Releasing seraphim
number 4.

528
00:26:00.910 --> 00:26:01.710
S-Shark!

529
00:26:05.460 --> 00:26:06.260
Deploy!

530
00:26:09.380 --> 00:26:11.130
If the World
Government has decided

531
00:26:11.130 --> 00:26:13.380
they want to kill me,
then I don't have much

532
00:26:13.430 --> 00:26:14.220
time left.

533
00:26:14.710 --> 00:26:18.040
CP0 is here, so I need
to pack my bags.

534
00:26:18.120 --> 00:26:22.690
Now please honor my re-quasar
and take me out to sea with you!

535
00:26:23.140 --> 00:26:26.370
You make it sound like we're all just
going on a picnic or something.

536
00:26:26.370 --> 00:26:28.460
If you disappear,
it'll be big news.

537
00:26:28.540 --> 00:26:31.480
This might put an even
bigger target on our backs.

538
00:26:33.210 --> 00:26:35.460
Okay. Your head looks
funny, so why not?

539
00:26:35.540 --> 00:26:37.120
How is that a reason?!

540
00:26:38.700 --> 00:26:39.600
Splendid!

541
00:26:39.680 --> 00:26:42.160
Somehow, I had
a feeling you'd say yes!

542
00:26:42.240 --> 00:26:44.180
Alright! Let us go!

543
00:26:44.260 --> 00:26:46.420
This will be a battlefield soon!

544
00:26:47.050 --> 00:26:50.940
For starters, please bring Bonney
to the Labophase above the clouds.

545
00:26:51.020 --> 00:26:52.580
How do we get up there?

546
00:26:52.660 --> 00:26:53.990
It should be easy.

547
00:26:54.070 --> 00:26:55.720
Just take the Vacuum Rocket.

548
00:26:55.800 --> 00:26:58.520
You can find it down here
in the Fabriophase phase.

549
00:26:58.600 --> 00:27:00.120
What's a Vacuum Rocket?

550
00:27:00.200 --> 00:27:01.200
That sounds cool!

551
00:27:02.480 --> 00:27:04.060
Well, don't dawdle now, boys!

552
00:27:04.140 --> 00:27:07.490
See you in the sky
in the blink of an eye!

553
00:27:09.120 --> 00:27:10.240
He disappeared!

554
00:27:11.230 --> 00:27:12.940
You're awesome,
Mister Apple Man!

555
00:27:13.670 --> 00:27:16.620
I'm finding the future
to be very confusing.

556
00:27:17.520 --> 00:27:19.960
Hey, take a gander at that!

557
00:27:20.040 --> 00:27:21.980
It's a giant monster!

558
00:27:34.800 --> 00:27:35.570
Dammit!

559
00:27:35.650 --> 00:27:36.880
It won't die!

560
00:27:38.040 --> 00:27:40.030
The bullets go right through it!

561
00:27:40.110 --> 00:27:41.310
Of course they do.

562
00:27:41.390 --> 00:27:45.120
This island is full of technical marvels
beyond your wildest imagination!

563
00:27:45.200 --> 00:27:48.730
If you think your guns will work
here, then you've been had!

564
00:27:49.240 --> 00:27:51.740
I've always wanted to fight
something like you.

565
00:27:51.820 --> 00:27:53.650
Something untouchable.

566
00:27:54.490 --> 00:27:56.790
And I know why they
couldn't hurt you.

567
00:27:56.870 --> 00:27:59.140
Because you're
from outer space!

568
00:27:59.220 --> 00:28:04.650
Prepare yourself, alien fiend!

569
00:28:12.200 --> 00:28:13.170
Tempest!

570
00:28:13.250 --> 00:28:14.050
What?

571
00:28:20.670 --> 00:28:23.390
It must have some sort
of space physiology!

572
00:28:23.470 --> 00:28:24.560
It's no use.

573
00:28:24.640 --> 00:28:26.050
I'm not giving up!

574
00:28:26.130 --> 00:28:26.980
Well, you should.

575
00:28:27.030 --> 00:28:27.970
It's a hologram.

576
00:28:28.050 --> 00:28:29.960
Why didn't you
tell me sooner?!

577
00:28:30.040 --> 00:28:32.360
Have you, perhaps,
been here before?

578
00:28:32.440 --> 00:28:34.350
Let's say it's nostalgic.

579
00:28:35.670 --> 00:28:37.360
Well, I'm already up here.

580
00:28:37.440 --> 00:28:41.020
I might as well check out whatever
this thing is above the clouds.

581
00:28:41.100 --> 00:28:43.750
Chances are, that's where
Vegapunk is hiding!

582
00:28:44.240 --> 00:28:47.150
Tell me, Lucci, do you see those
yellow lines way up there?

583
00:28:47.150 --> 00:28:48.000
In the clouds?

584
00:28:48.080 --> 00:28:49.710
Ah. Yes.

585
00:28:51.850 --> 00:28:54.500
Watch what happens when
someone crosses them.

586
00:29:02.170 --> 00:29:04.850
Laser beams automatically
fire on them.

587
00:29:09.110 --> 00:29:11.720
It's a defensive system
called the Frontier Dome.

588
00:29:11.800 --> 00:29:15.280
It encircles the Labophase,
guarding in all directions.

589
00:29:18.720 --> 00:29:22.920
The lesson here is not to underestimate
the world's greatest scientist.

590
00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:24.980
You really should've
told him that.

591
00:29:25.060 --> 00:29:26.220
Stussy!

592
00:29:26.300 --> 00:29:29.180
How could you just stand
there and watch me fry?

593
00:29:30.560 --> 00:29:32.280
Warms you up
faster than tea!

594
00:29:41.070 --> 00:29:44.130
You think you
can come into my lab?!

595
00:29:44.670 --> 00:29:45.910
And be more violent?!

596
00:29:49.230 --> 00:29:50.430
Punk-ass pigs!

597
00:29:53.850 --> 00:29:55.070
Ultra...!

598
00:29:56.630 --> 00:29:59.230
Alright, this place
is officially insane.

599
00:29:59.310 --> 00:30:01.010
Is that one a hologram, too?

600
00:30:01.560 --> 00:30:02.420
Oh, no.

601
00:30:02.500 --> 00:30:03.970
This young lady is Atlas.

602
00:30:04.450 --> 00:30:06.080
She's one of the Vegapunks.

603
00:30:06.160 --> 00:30:06.860
Look!

604
00:30:08.050 --> 00:30:08.850
It's Atlas!

605
00:30:09.300 --> 00:30:09.610
Atlas!

606
00:30:09.610 --> 00:30:11.210
Abort mission immediately!

607
00:30:11.290 --> 00:30:12.120
Mighty!

608
00:30:13.250 --> 00:30:14.440
Very well then.

609
00:30:14.520 --> 00:30:15.320
Hey!

610
00:30:22.910 --> 00:30:24.730
Six-king pistol!

611
00:30:31.200 --> 00:30:32.000
Oh, no!

612
00:30:32.080 --> 00:30:32.780
Atlas!

613
00:30:32.810 --> 00:30:34.070
She's down!

614
00:30:34.150 --> 00:30:36.110
Merciless as ever, isn't he?

615
00:30:50.960 --> 00:30:52.180
He beat her in one shot!

616
00:30:52.260 --> 00:30:53.900
This guy's seriously scary!

617
00:30:53.980 --> 00:30:54.830
What's going on?

618
00:30:54.910 --> 00:30:56.760
Why is Cipher Pol
attacking us?

619
00:30:56.840 --> 00:31:00.330
We both work for the Government,
so we're allies, aren't we?

620
00:31:00.410 --> 00:31:02.030
Attention, Fabriophase!

621
00:31:02.110 --> 00:31:04.120
Evacuate the lab immediately!

622
00:31:09.310 --> 00:31:10.130
Evacuate now!

623
00:31:10.130 --> 00:31:10.990
An evacuation notice?

624
00:31:10.990 --> 00:31:11.970
We have to go!

625
00:31:12.050 --> 00:31:13.010
Run to the factory!

626
00:31:14.340 --> 00:31:15.040
Evacuate now!

627
00:31:15.100 --> 00:31:16.570
We are under attack!

628
00:31:19.600 --> 00:31:21.660
She's still alive, but barely.

629
00:31:21.740 --> 00:31:24.680
Let's eliminate her while
we have the opportunity.

630
00:31:27.510 --> 00:31:31.770
First we gotta find it,
then we fly!

631
00:31:43.150 --> 00:31:44.580
Straw hat.

632
00:31:47.420 --> 00:31:48.320
Pigeon guy!
